# LIFX Lighting Schedule
# Supercronic logs all output to stdout/stderr automatically
# Times run in the TZ configured in .env
#
# Crontab entries call lifx.py directly. Address lights by --ip: it talks to
# the bulb directly instead of relying on discovery broadcasts, which some
# bulbs ignore. Keep the table below mapping each IP to its light name.
#
# Jobs on the same minute run in parallel, so put lights that change together
# on one line - repeat --ip for lights sharing values, and chain lights with
# different values with `;`.
#
# Use --verify on scheduled jobs: it reads state back and retries until the
# lights match (exit code non-zero if they don't).
#
# Lights (use fixed IPs - DHCP reservations on the router):
#   192.168.1.10  Office
#   192.168.1.11  Desk
#
# Examples (uncomment / edit to build the schedule):
#
# Evening: turn on (if off) and set warm white, fading in over 2s
# 0 18 * * * lifx.py set --ip 192.168.1.10 --ip 192.168.1.11 --saturation 0 --brightness 45875 --kelvin 3000 --duration 2000 --on --verify
#
# Late night: dim without --on, so lights someone turned off stay off
# 0 21 * * * lifx.py set --ip 192.168.1.10 --brightness 13107 --duration 2000 --verify; lifx.py set --ip 192.168.1.11 --brightness 6554 --duration 2000 --verify
#
# Morning: power off
# 0 7 * * * lifx.py off --ip 192.168.1.10 --ip 192.168.1.11 --duration 1000 --verify
